==District 3==
{{see also|Washington's 3rd congressional district}}
The 3rd congressional district encompasses the southernmost portion of [[Western Washington|western]] and [[central Washington]]. It includes the counties of [[Lewis County, Washington|Lewis]], [[Pacific County, Washington|Pacific]], [[Wahkiakum County, Washington|Wahkiakum]], [[Cowlitz County, Washington|Cowlitz]], [[Clark County, Washington|Clark]], [[Skamania County, Washington|Skamania]], and [[Klickitat County, Washington|Klickitat]], and a small sliver of southern [[Thurston County, Washington|Thurston]] county. The district has a [[Cook Partisan Voting Index|PVI]] of R+4. The incumbent is Republican [[Jaime Herrera Beutler]], who has represented the district since 2011. She was re-elected with 62% of the vote in 2016.
