==District 4==
{{see also|Washington's 4th congressional district}}
The 4th congressional district is located in [[central Washington]], covering the counties of, [[Douglas County, Washington|Douglas]], [[Okanogan County, Washington|Okanogan]], [[Grant County, Washington|Grant]], [[Yakima County, Washington|Yakima]], [[Franklin County, Washington|Franklin]], [[Benton County, Washington|Benton]], and [[Adams County, Washington|Adams]]. The district is dominated by the [[Yakima]] and [[Tri-Cities, Washington|Tri-Cities]] areas. The district has a [[Cook Partisan Voting Index|PVI]] of R+13. The incumbent is Republican [[Dan Newhouse]], who has represented the district since 2015. He was re-elected with 58% of the vote in 2016.
