==District 8==
{{see also|Washington's 8th congressional district}}
The 8th congressional district includes the eastern portions of [[King County, Washington|King]] and [[Pierce County, Washington|Pierce]] counties and crosses the [[Cascade mountains]] to include [[Chelan County, Washington|Chelan]] and [[Kittitas County, Washington|Kittitas]] counties.  The population centers on the west side of the mountains include the exurban communities of [[Sammamish, Washington|Sammamish]], [[Issaquah, Washington|Issaquah]], and [[Auburn, Washington|Auburn]].  On the east side, the 8th's population centers are rural communities [[Wenatchee, Washington|Wenatchee]], [[Leavenworth, Washington|Leavenworth]], and [[Ellensburg, Washington|Ellensburg]]. The district has a [[Cook Partisan Voting Index|PVI]] of EVEN. The incumbent is Republican [[Dave Reichert]], who has represented the district since 2005. He was re-elected with 60% of the vote in 2016.

Reichert is retiring.<ref name=reichertwontrun>{{cite web|url=http://www.seattletimes.com/seattle-news/politics/u-s-rep-dave-reichert-says-he-wont-run-for-re-election/|title=U.S. Rep. Dave Reichert says he won’t run for re-election|work=[[The Seattle Times]]|last=Brunner|first=Jim|date=September 6, 2017|accessdate=September 6, 2017}}</ref>

